</Content></Shape1><Shape2><Type>msoPicture</Type><Content>Picture 4</Content></Shape2><Shape3><Type>msoPicture</Type><Content>Picture 5</Content></Shape3><Shape4><Type>msoPicture</Type><Content>Picture 6</Content></Shape4></Shapes></Slide15><Slide16><Transitions><Transition>ppEffectNone</Transition></Transitions><Animations /><Shapes><Shape0><Type>msoPlaceholder</Type><Content>Spacing</Content></Shape0><Shape1><Type>msoPlaceholder</Type><Content>Text and images kept within a reasonable distance from the edges of the slide. This prevents the slide from looking over-crowded. </Content></Shape1><Shape2><Type>msoPicture</Type><Content>Picture 4</Content></Shape2><Shape3><Type>msoPicture</Type><Content>Picture 5</Content></Shape3></Shapes></Slide16><Slide17><Transitions><Transition>ppEffectNone</Transition></Transitions><Animations /><Shapes><Shape0><Type>msoPlaceholder</Type><Content>Easy to Read</Content></Shape0><Shape1><Type>msoPlaceholder</Type><Content>Slides that are easy to read. Avoid flashy color schemes, fonts, and animation. These features should complement a presentation, and not be the presentation itself. </Content></Shape1><Shape2><Type>msoPicture</Type><Content>Picture 4</Content></Shape2><Shape3><Type>msoPicture</Type><Content>Picture 5</Content></Shape3></Shapes></Slide17><Slide18><Transitions><Transition>ppEffectNone</Transition></Transitions><Animations><Effect>msoAnimEffectStretch</Effect></Animations><Shapes><Shape0><Type>msoAutoShape</Type><Content>A picture is
